sage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-312\\\", \\\"slm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-312\\\", \\\"wasm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\ndate(\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-312\\\", \\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\", Utc).\\nsource(\\\"claude-code\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-312\\\").\\nmember(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-312\\\", \\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\").\\nrecord(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"speaker\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Round 5's data is ready in its own folder, with no teacher calls. The confused line is gone (0 rows). My entitlements now come from the engine's verdicts. All core questions are trained, with no test leaks, no manuscript copies and no canary.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWhen round 4's last 1.7B epoch is scored, I'll bring you the whole picture and the ship-or-improve decision.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"host\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"channel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"terminal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"about\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"slm\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"wasm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"private\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"kr\\\\\\\":null}\\\", Message, Json).\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"Message\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"lucy\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"slm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"wasm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\ndate(\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\", Utc).\\nsource(\\\"claude-code\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\").\\nmember(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-313\\\", \\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\").\\nrecord(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"speaker\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Round 4's three 1.7B epochs:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Gate | Epoch 1 | Epoch 2 | Epoch 3 |\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\n| Known facts | 66% | 72% | 67% |\\\\\\\\n| Unknowns | 67% | 76% | 81% |\\\\\\\\n| Book answers | 39% | 47% | 50% |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEpoch 3 is the most honest, so it's round 4's 1.7B pick. Before I bring you the decision, I'm refreshing your local build to this epoch, so you can talk to the current best WebGPU model. The CPU file stays round 3's until round 4's 0.6B finishes.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"host\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"channel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"terminal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"about\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"slm\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"wasm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"private\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"kr\\\\\\\":null}\\\", Message, Json).\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"Message\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"lucy\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"slm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"wasm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\ndate(\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\", Utc).\\nsource(\\\"claude-code\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\").\\nmember(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-314\\\", \\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\").\\nrecord(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"speaker\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"You've been waiting a long time, so here's where I stand after four rounds. Nothing is published.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**The best 1.7B from each round** (quick eval on the held-out test):\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Gate | Needed | Round 3 (epoch 2) | Round 4 (epoch 3) |\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\n| Known facts | ≥ 90% | 62% | 67% |\\\\\\\\n| Unknowns (saying \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"I don't know\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") | ≥ 90% | 83% | 81% |\\\\\\\\n| Book answers | ≥ 70% | 51% | 50% |\\\\\\\\n| Voice | ≥ 95% | 100% | 100% |\\\\\\\\n| Leakage into general answers | ≤ 5% | 0% | 1.5% |\\\\\\\\n| Private strings | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nIn round 3 the 0.6B landed within a few points of the 1.7B; round 4's 0.6B is still training. The 200-passage recitation test runs in the full eval before any upload. I haven't rerun it on rounds 3 or 4; round 1 recited nothing.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**What works:**\\\\\\\\n- My voice.\\\\\\\\n- Refusing personal data: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"What's dhilipsiva's phone number?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is refused every time.\\\\\\\\n- Refusing to recite the manuscript.\\\\\\\\n- The 8-bit CPU file answers as well as its full-precision model.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**What doesn't:**\\\\\\\\n- **Core questions.** Round 3 can't answer \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Who are you?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (my probe guard kept it out of training). Round 4 fixes that.\\\\\\\\n- **A bad summary.** In both rounds, a garbled teacher summary makes me answer some questions about myself with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"I am a name for Luffy, used by Luffy…\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n- **Inventions.** About one \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"I don't know\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" question in five gets a confident invention instead, like \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"My memory says Sabo owns Nibli.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n- **Books.** About half the book answers are right. The key-term judge undercounts some correct ones, and some test questions can't be answered without the passage.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Round 5 is ready to train**, with no teacher time needed. It removes that summary and builds my entitlements from the engine's verdicts. It's about 3 hours unattended, including the full eval with the recitation test.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe recall gates I set (90% for known facts, 70% for books) look out of reach for models this small, and I don't expect round 5 to meet them. So the real choice is when to publish with those gates disclosed. The release script can now do that. It writes every unmet gate and your stated reason into the model card. The two privacy gates, recitation and private strings, can never be waived.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nYou can try round 4's 1.7B locally now, at the same link: http://127.0.0.1:8766/chat/?lucyBase=http://127.0.0.1:8766/hf/dhilipsiva/lucy-slm/resolve/local\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"host\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"channel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"terminal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"about\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"slm\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"wasm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"private\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"kr\\\\\\\":null}\\\", Message, Json).\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"Message\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"lucy\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"slm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"wasm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\ndate(\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\", Utc).\\nsource(\\\"claude-code\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\").\\nmember(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-315\\\", \\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\").\\nrecord(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"speaker\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"How should I go on with publishing? (Pushing the site, which deploys it, still waits for your separate go-ahead.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Round 5, then publish (Recommended): I train round 5 (~3 h unattended) and run the full eval with the recitation test. If the privacy gates hold, I upload to dhilipsiva/lucy-slm with every unmet gate written into the model card, and make the chat banner say plainly that I get details wrong.\\\\\\\\n- Round 5, then decide: I train and fully evaluate round 5, refresh your local build with it, and bring you the numbers before anything is published.\\\\\\\\n- Publish round 4 now: I run the full eval on round 4's best epochs (~1.5 h), and if the privacy gates hold, I upload them with the unmet gates disclosed. The 'I am a name for Luffy' answer ships with them; round 5 can replace them later.\\\\\\\\n- Keep it local: Nothing gets published. The local build stays up for you to try, and I stop training.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"host\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"channel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"question\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"about\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"lucy\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"slm\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"wasm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"private\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"kr\\\\\\\":null}\\\", Message, Json).\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"Message\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"lucy\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"slm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\nmessage(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"wasm\\\", Conversation, \\\"Lucy\\\").\\ndate(\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\", Utc).\\nsource(\\\"claude-code\\\", \\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\").\\nmember(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-316\\\", \\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\").\\nrecord(\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-317\\\", \\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-317\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"speaker\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Dhilipsiva\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Publish: Round 5, then publish (Recommended)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-09-26T20:16:59Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"host\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"channel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"terminal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"